* stata.toc -- content file for the powerape Stata port
* Point -net from- at the repository (or at a local copy of it):
*   . net from "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jespernwulff/powerape-stata/main/"
*   . net describe powerape
*   . net install powerape
*   . net get powerape                        (ancillary files: showcase.do and build.do)
*   . mata: mata mlib index                   (index the newly installed Mata library)
v 3
d powerape for Stata: power analysis for average partial effects (APE) and average interaction effects (AIE)
d Stata port of the R package powerape (https://github.com/jespernwulff/powerape)
d Jesper N. Wulff, Aarhus University
d
d Simulation-based power for the APE/AIE of probit and logit models: minimum-effect,
d detection and equivalence claims; power curves; required n; minimum detectable effects;
d robustness sweeps; justified alpha; citable power statements. Every simulated study is
d fit, by default, by Stata's own probit/logit/cfprobit (engine(stata)); engine(mata) is a
d fast self-contained Mata engine. Stata 16 or later (see the package description).
d
p powerape Power analysis for APEs and AIEs of probit/logit models (ado, help file, Mata library)
